6. CONTACT FORM: MESSAGES MUST GO TO THE ADMIN DASHBOARD
==================================================

THIS IS A CRITICAL BUSINESS REQUIREMENT.

When a visitor submits the Contact Form, the message must be stored in MongoDB and become visible inside the existing Admin Dashboard.

IMPORTANT:

DO NOT SEND CONTACT FORM MESSAGES TO EMAIL.

DO NOT USE SMTP FOR CONTACT FORM DELIVERY.

DO NOT USE RESEND FOR CONTACT FORM DELIVERY.

DO NOT SEND THE CONTACT MESSAGE TO THE BUSINESS OWNER'S EMAIL.

The destination of the contact form submission is the application's own database-backed Admin Message Management System.

EXPECTED WORKFLOW:

1. Visitor opens /contact.
2. Visitor completes the contact form.
3. Visitor clicks Submit.
4. Frontend validates the form.
5. Frontend sends the message to the actual Express backend.
6. Backend validates and sanitizes the submitted information.
7. Backend creates a new contact message record in MongoDB.
8. Backend returns a successful response.
9. Frontend displays a polished success notification or success state.
10. Admin can open the Admin Dashboard.
11. Admin navigates to the Contact Messages section.
12. Admin sees the newly submitted message.

The entire workflow must use actual backend and database integration.

Do not simulate message submission.

Do not use LocalStorage as the message database.

Do not create an in-memory message store.

Do not show success unless the database operation succeeds.

